module

public import TauCeti.AlgebraicGeometry.Curves.StableReduction.NumericalType.Basic
public import TauCeti.AlgebraicGeometry.IntersectionNumber.Weight

/-!
# The numerical type of a regular model

Let `R` be a local ring of dimension at most one whose maximal ideal is generated by a
nonzerodivisor `π`, for instance a discrete valuation ring with a uniformizer, with residue field
`k`, and let `X` be a regular Noetherian integral scheme, proper and flat over `R`, all of whose
points have codimension at most two, such as a proper regular model of a curve over `R`. Let
`Cᵢ` be the irreducible components of the special fibre, with their reduced structures, and
suppose that `H⁰` and `H¹` of the structure sheaf of every `Cᵢ` are finite-dimensional over `k`.

When the special fibre is connected, the data

* the multiplicities `mᵢ` of the components in the special fibre
  (`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom.specialFiberMultiplicity`),
* the weights `wᵢ = [κᵢ : k]` of their constant fields `κᵢ = H⁰(Cᵢ, 𝒪_{Cᵢ})`
  (`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom.specialFiberWeight`),
* the intersection matrix `aᵢⱼ = (Cⱼ · Cᵢ)`
  (`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom.specialFiberIntersectionMatrix`), and
* the genera `gᵢ = dim_{κᵢ} H¹(Cᵢ, 𝒪_{Cᵢ})` of the components over their constant fields

form a numerical type in the sense of [Stacks, Tag 0C6Z](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0C6Z),
the **numerical type of the regular model**
(`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom.specialFiberNumericalType`). Its weighted Picard group
`TauCeti.NumericalType.Pic` and signed genus `TauCeti.NumericalType.arithmeticGenus` are the
combinatorial invariants through which the prime-to-residue-characteristic Picard torsion of the
generic fibre controls the special fibre in the proof of semistable reduction in genus at least
two ([Stacks, Tag 0CEI](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0CEI)).

Connectedness of the special fibre is a hypothesis here. It is exactly the connectedness axiom of
the numerical type
(`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom.isPreconnected_preimage_closedPoint_iff_reflTransGen`), and over a
discrete valuation ring it holds for instance when the generic fibre is geometrically connected,
by Zariski's connectedness theorem. The genera are taken over the constant fields `κᵢ` rather than
over `k`, and are not the genera of the normalizations of the `Cᵢ`; over `k` they give
`dim_k H¹(Cᵢ, 𝒪_{Cᵢ}) = wᵢ gᵢ`
(`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom.specialFiberWeight_mul_finrank_cohomology_one`).

## Main declarations

* `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom.specialFiberNumericalType`: the numerical type of the special
  fibre of a regular model, with its data described by
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom.specialFiberNumericalType_multiplicity`,
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom.specialFiberNumericalType_weight`,
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom.specialFiberNumericalType_intersection` and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom.specialFiberNumericalType_genus`.

## References

* [The Stacks Project, Tag 0C6Z](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0C6Z), for numerical types,
  and [Section 55.9](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0C9U), for the numerical type attached to
  a regular model.
* Q. Liu, *Algebraic Geometry and Arithmetic Curves*, Section 9.1.
-/

public section

noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory AlgebraicGeometry IsLocalRing Order
open TauCeti TauCeti.AlgebraicGeometry TauCeti.AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules
open AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.IdealSheafData (vanishingIdeal)

universe u

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom

variable {R : Type u} [CommRing R] [IsLocalRing R] [Ring.DimensionLEOne R]
  {X : Scheme.{u}} (toBase : X ⟶ Spec (.of R)) [IsIntegral X] [IsNoetherian X]
  [TauCeti.AlgebraicGeometry.IsRegular X] [IsProper toBase] [Flat toBase]
  (hX : ∀ x : X, coheight x ≤ 2) (hη : toBase (genericPoint X) ≠ closedPoint R)
  (h₀ : ∀ (η : CodimensionOnePoint X) (hc : toBase η = closedPoint R),
    letI := subschemeOverResidueField
      (toBase.ker_specialFiberι_le_vanishingIdeal_closure_singleton hc)
    FiniteDimensional (ResidueField R) (Cohomology (InvertibleSheaf.trivial
      (vanishingIdeal ⟨closure {(η : X)}, isClosed_closure⟩).subscheme).obj 0))
  (h₁ : ∀ (η : CodimensionOnePoint X) (hc : toBase η = closedPoint R),
    letI := subschemeOverResidueField
      (toBase.ker_specialFiberι_le_vanishingIdeal_closure_singleton hc)
    FiniteDimensional (ResidueField R) (Cohomology (InvertibleSheaf.trivial
      (vanishingIdeal ⟨closure {(η : X)}, isClosed_closure⟩).subscheme).obj 1))
  {π : R} (hπ : maximalIdeal R = Ideal.span {π}) (hreg : IsSMulRegular R π)
  (hconn : _root_.IsPreconnected (toBase ⁻¹' {closedPoint R}))

/-- **The numerical type of a regular model.** Let `X` be a regular Noetherian integral scheme,
proper and flat over a local ring `R` of dimension at most one whose maximal ideal is generated by
a nonzerodivisor `π`, with all points of codimension at most two and generic point away from the
closed point. Suppose that `H⁰` and `H¹` of the structure sheaf of every component `Cᵢ` of the
special fibre are finite-dimensional over the residue field `k`, and that the special fibre is
connected. Its numerical type ([Stacks, Tag 0C6Z](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0C6Z)) has
the components of the special fibre as its components, with

* multiplicity `mᵢ` the multiplicity of `Cᵢ` in the divisor of `π`,
* weight `wᵢ = [κᵢ : k]` the degree of the constant field `κᵢ = H⁰(Cᵢ, 𝒪_{Cᵢ})`,
* intersection matrix `aᵢⱼ = (Cⱼ · Cᵢ)`, and
* genus `gᵢ = dim_{κᵢ} H¹(Cᵢ, 𝒪_{Cᵢ})`, the arithmetic genus of `Cᵢ` over its constant field.

The definition is exposed so that the component type is the finite set of codimension-one points
of the special fibre indexing `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom.specialFiberIntersectionMatrix`. -/
@[expose]
def specialFiberNumericalType : NumericalType.{u} where
  Component := (toBase.finite_setOf_base_eq_closedPoint
    (toBase.maximalIdeal_ne_bot_of_base_ne_closedPoint hη) hη).toFinset
  componentDecidableEq := Classical.decEq _
  componentNonempty := by
    obtain ⟨η, hc⟩ := toBase.exists_codimensionOnePoint_base_eq_closedPoint hη
    exact ⟨⟨η, (Set.Finite.mem_toFinset _).mpr hc⟩⟩
  multiplicity j := ⟨toBase.specialFiberMultiplicity π j,
    toBase.specialFiberMultiplicity_pos hη (hπ ▸ Ideal.mem_span_singleton_self π)
      (toBase.ne_zero_of_base_ne_closedPoint hη hπ) j ((Set.Finite.mem_toFinset _).mp j.2)⟩
  weight i := ⟨toBase.specialFiberWeight ((Set.Finite.mem_toFinset _).mp i.2),
    toBase.specialFiberWeight_pos _ (h₀ i ((Set.Finite.mem_toFinset _).mp i.2))⟩
  intersection := toBase.specialFiberIntersectionMatrix hX hη
  intersection_isSymm := toBase.specialFiberIntersectionMatrix_isSymm hX hη h₀ h₁
  offDiagonal_nonneg _ _ := toBase.specialFiberIntersectionMatrix_nonneg_of_ne hX hη h₀ h₁
  connected := toBase.specialFiberIntersectionMatrix_reflTransGen hX hη h₀ h₁ hconn
  fiber_relation i := by
    have h := congrFun
      (toBase.specialFiberIntersectionMatrix_mulVec_specialFiberMultiplicity hX hη h₀ h₁ hπ hreg) i
    simpa [Matrix.mulVec, dotProduct, mul_comm] using h
  weight_dvd := toBase.specialFiberWeight_dvd_specialFiberIntersectionMatrix hX hη
  genus i := Module.finrank
    Γ((vanishingIdeal ⟨closure {((i : CodimensionOnePoint X) : X)}, isClosed_closure⟩).subscheme, ⊤)
    (Cohomology (InvertibleSheaf.trivial (vanishingIdeal
      ⟨closure {((i : CodimensionOnePoint X) : X)}, isClosed_closure⟩).subscheme).obj 1)

/-- The multiplicity of a component of the numerical type of a regular model is its multiplicity
in the divisor of `π`. -/
@[simp]
theorem specialFiberNumericalType_multiplicity
    (i : (toBase.finite_setOf_base_eq_closedPoint
      (toBase.maximalIdeal_ne_bot_of_base_ne_closedPoint hη) hη).toFinset) :
    ((toBase.specialFiberNumericalType hX hη h₀ h₁ hπ hreg hconn).multiplicity i : ℕ) =
      toBase.specialFiberMultiplicity π i :=
  rfl

/-- The weight of a component of the numerical type of a regular model is the degree
`dim_k H⁰(C, 𝒪_C)` of its constant field over the residue field. -/
@[simp]
theorem specialFiberNumericalType_weight
    (i : (toBase.finite_setOf_base_eq_closedPoint
      (toBase.maximalIdeal_ne_bot_of_base_ne_closedPoint hη) hη).toFinset) :
    ((toBase.specialFiberNumericalType hX hη h₀ h₁ hπ hreg hconn).weight i : ℕ) =
      toBase.specialFiberWeight ((Set.Finite.mem_toFinset _).mp i.2) :=
  rfl

/-- The intersection matrix of the numerical type of a regular model is the intersection matrix
of its special fibre. -/
@[simp]
theorem specialFiberNumericalType_intersection :
    (toBase.specialFiberNumericalType hX hη h₀ h₁ hπ hreg hconn).intersection =
      toBase.specialFiberIntersectionMatrix hX hη :=
  rfl

/-- The genus of a component `C` of the numerical type of a regular model is
`dim_{κ_C} H¹(C, 𝒪_C)`, over the ring `κ_C = H⁰(C, 𝒪_C)` of global functions on `C`, which is its
constant field. -/
@[simp]
theorem specialFiberNumericalType_genus
    (i : (toBase.finite_setOf_base_eq_closedPoint
      (toBase.maximalIdeal_ne_bot_of_base_ne_closedPoint hη) hη).toFinset) :
    (toBase.specialFiberNumericalType hX hη h₀ h₁ hπ hreg hconn).genus i = Module.finrank
      Γ((vanishingIdeal ⟨closure {((i : CodimensionOnePoint X) : X)}, isClosed_closure⟩).subscheme,
        ⊤)
      (Cohomology (InvertibleSheaf.trivial
        (vanishingIdeal ⟨closure {((i : CodimensionOnePoint X) : X)},
          isClosed_closure⟩).subscheme).obj 1) :=
  rfl

end AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom

end
